      "math_academy_id": "q-108297",
      "sequence_position": 15,
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$ Given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(6),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\le x)=0.05.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |\n| $6$ | $\\,0.676\\,$ | $\\,0.872\\,$ | $\\,1.237\\,$ | $\\,1.635\\,$ | $\\,2.204\\,$ |\n| $7$ | $\\,0.989\\,$ | $\\,1.239\\,$ | $\\,1.690\\,$ | $\\,2.167\\,$ | $\\,2.833\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X>x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.05 \\\\  & =0.95\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{χ}^{2}(6),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=6.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $6$ | $\\,0.676\\,$ | $\\,0.872\\,$ | $\\,1.237\\,$ | $\\,1.635\\,$ | $\\,2.204\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>1.635)=0.950.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=1.635.$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
